# Trivy misconfiguration suppressions — every entry MUST have a justification.
# Format: <AVD-ID>  # reason

# WireGuard UDP/51820 on the sandbox NSG is intentionally open to 0.0.0.0/0.
# A home broadband IP is dynamic and can't be pinned to a CIDR in advance.
# WireGuard's own cryptographic handshake authenticates every connection —
# this is a single authenticated-VPN port, not an unauthenticated management
# port (unlike SSH/RDP, which this repo never opens to the internet).
# See infra/modules/network/main.tf — azurerm_network_security_group.sandbox
AVD-AZU-0047
